## 7. Optional C-Phasing plots

These commands were also commented out in the supplied script. Run them only when these additional outputs are needed.

### 7.1 Generate a 500-kb matrix

```bash
cphasing pairs2cool \
    CLv5.pairs.gz \
    CLv5.T2T.contigsizes \
    CLv5.500k.cool \
    -bs 500k \
    -t 60
```

### 7.2 Plot a balanced genome-wide map

```bash
cphasing plot \
    -m CLv5.500k.cool \
    --only-chr \
    --chr-prefix Chr \
    --balance \
    -o CLv5.genome_wide.png \
    --dpi 600
```

### 7.3 Plot balanced per-chromosome maps

```bash
cphasing plot \
    -m CLv5.10k.cool \
    --only-chr \
    --chr-prefix Chr \
    --per-chromosome \
    --balance \
    -o CLv5.per_chr.png \
    --dpi 600
```

These examples request matrix balancing and select chromosomes using the `Chr` prefix. Adjust the prefix to match the FASTA identifiers. Balanced plots and the custom script's requested raw-mode plot should be distinguished when reporting results.

## Main output files

| File | Description |
| :--- | :--- |
| `CLv5.T2T.fa.fai` | FASTA index |
| `CLv5.T2T.contigsizes` | Reference sequence lengths |
| `CLv5.porec.gz` | Expected Pore-C mapping table in the supplied workflow |
| `CLv5.pairs.gz` | Pairwise contact records |
| `CLv5.10k.cool` | Contact matrix at 10-kb resolution |
| `CLv5.q5.10k.all_chr.png` | Heatmap from the custom plotting script |
| `CLv5.500k.cool` | Optional contact matrix at 500-kb resolution |

The workflow documents mapping and visualization against an existing assembly. It does not run chromosome scaffolding or haplotype phasing. Interpret contact patterns together with the actual read accession, mapping quality, coverage and independent assembly evidence.

